 QuotePath←{
⍝ Takes a path and returns it ready to become part of a Git command: in double-quotes.\\
⍝ Quoting is not just about blanks: on Windows the command line is split before Git ever
⍝ sees it, while everywhere else the command goes through a shell, where a path holding
⍝ `$`, `&`, `;` or a bracket would be interpreted. It also stops the shell from expanding
⍝ a wildcard against the wrong directory - Git resolves a pathspec against the project.\\
⍝ Any double-quotes around the path are removed first: a path that came from Git is quoted
⍝ already (see `UnquotePath`), and `git add ""APLSource/Has Blanks.aplf""` fails.
     0=≢⍵:⍵
     '"',(⍵~'"'),'"'
 }
